Consider the following C function definition:
```c
int compute(int n) {
    static int acc = 2;
    if (n <= 0) return 1;
    acc += n;
    int sub = compute(n - 2);
    return acc + sub;
}
```
Note carefully that `acc + sub` is evaluated AFTER the recursive call `compute(n - 2)` returns (so `acc` holds its final mutated static value across all unwinding stack frames!). What is the exact integer value returned by calling `compute(5)`?

